Fovea eBPF programs in this directory are dual-licensed under:

    MIT OR GPL-2.0-only

You may use each file under either license at your option.

Every `*.bpf.c` file must carry:

    // SPDX-License-Identifier: (MIT OR GPL-2.0-only)

and must declare this exact Linux BPF runtime license string:

    char LICENSE[] SEC("license") = "Dual MIT/GPL";

The runtime declaration is part of the program's kernel-loading contract. It
does not replace the source file's SPDX license declaration.

The MIT license text is available in the repository root `LICENSE` file. The
GPL-2.0-only license text is published by the Free Software Foundation and the
Linux kernel project.
